Loops are used when you want to repeat something multiple times instead of writing the same code again and again.

there are the 3 diff types of loops 

1 for loop 
2 while loop 
3 do while loop
4 for...of loop 
5 for...in loop 

the diff between loops in javascript and there use case how they diff in diff condtion 

| "Situation"       |" Use "                 |
| ----------------- | ---------------------- |
| Fixed count       | `for`                  |
| Unknown condition | `while`                |
| Arrays            | `for...of` or `.map()` |
| Objects           | `for...in`             |
| Async operations  | `for...of`             |

 this is how we use the loop in backend 
Loops = repeat logic
Backend = heavy use of loops for data
Use for...of for async operations
Prefer .map(), .filter() for clean code



